<title>SWEDEN: Saab Automobile U.S. Jan car sales down.</title>
<headline>Saab Automobile U.S. Jan car sales down.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saab Automobile AB said on Tuesday its U.S. car sales in January fell 12.6 percent to 1,361 vehicles compared to the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The sales were, however, around the average of 1,379 cars sold in the U.S. by the company during the 1990s, Saab Automobile said in a statement.</p>
<p>The most popular model was the Saab 900 whose five door version accounted for nearly 50 percent of the month's total sales.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
